      <memberdef kind="function" id="classAstValueAttribute_1a29f4bc1846bc95610c3098cd904cff9b" prot="public" static="no" const="yes" explicit="no" inline="yes" virt="virtual">
        <type><ref refid="classAstAttribute" kindref="compound">AstAttribute</ref> *</type>
        <definition>virtual AstAttribute* AstValueAttribute&lt; T &gt;::copy</definition>
        <argsstring>() const override</argsstring>
        <name>copy</name>
        <reimplements refid="classAstAttribute_1afde475da251d23d4b873550fce74881a">copy</reimplements>
        <reimplementedby refid="classAstSgNodeAttribute_1a2c0d1fdfbd0148202d7fec2854c99096">copy</reimplementedby>
        <reimplementedby refid="classAstSgNodeListAttribute_1ac097332d16a4942c2d6cc6822e39e72b">copy</reimplementedby>
        <reimplementedby refid="classAstIntAttribute_1ae4c9b457510f1f45b2f554d2549d2ea2">copy</reimplementedby>
        <briefdescription>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>Virtual copy constructor.</para><para>Copy-constructs a new object on the heap and returns its pointer. All subclasses must implement this in order to instantiate the correct dynamic type, although many don&apos;t. If this <ref refid="classAstValueAttribute_1a29f4bc1846bc95610c3098cd904cff9b" kindref="member">copy</ref> method returns a null pointer (like the base implementation) then the attribute is not copied as part of copying its container. E.g., an attribute stored in an AST will not be copied when the AST is copied if that attribute is directly derived from <ref refid="classAstAttribute" kindref="compound">AstAttribute</ref> and fails to implement <ref refid="classAstValueAttribute_1a29f4bc1846bc95610c3098cd904cff9b" kindref="member">copy</ref>. If a subclass fails to implement <ref refid="classAstValueAttribute_1a29f4bc1846bc95610c3098cd904cff9b" kindref="member">copy</ref> and inherits from a class that does implement a <ref refid="classAstValueAttribute_1a29f4bc1846bc95610c3098cd904cff9b" kindref="member">copy</ref> that returns non-null, then the copied attribute will have an incorrect dynamic type.</para><para>It would be nice if we could make this pure virtual, but unfortunately ROSETTA-generated code fails to compile because it generates an instantiation of this interface (whether or not that code is ever executed is unkown). [Robb Matzke 2015-11-10] </para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
        </inbodydescription>
        <location file="/home/liao6/workspace/rose-github/src/midend/astProcessing/AstAttributeMechanism.h" line="466" column="1" bodyfile="/home/liao6/workspace/rose-github/src/midend/astProcessing/AstAttributeMechanism.h" bodystart="466" bodyend="466"/>
      </memberdef>
